      "content": "okay, that makes more sense, thanks. so you're saying it's about the convolution in the frequency domain.\n\nif the windowing is basically convolving the signal's spectrum with the transform of the window, then how does choosing a specific window (like a Hamming vs a rectangular one) actually help with those \"spikes\" i was talking about? \n\ni'm still trying to wrap my head around how the mathematical shape of the window prevents those weird, tiny disruptions from spreading out and looking like real signal components. like, what is happening inside the math to stop that \"leakage\"?",
